    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552">

                <pb facs="0721" n="707" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg707"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.8951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Berle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-14T19:00:00-03:00">May 14, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1520. For Truslow and Utz,<anchor n="84" xml:id="d552-f1"/> RDC, from McLaughlin
                    and Korkegi.<anchor n="85" xml:id="d552-f2"/> Extension rubber agreement not yet
                    signed. Bouças holding up as trading point in obtaining further concessions
                    Brazil nuts. We expect he will make his Brazil nut position clear tomorrow. I
                    pointed out that if his Brazil nut position is unacceptable RDC and Department
                    may find it necessary to review rubber agreement extension offer. [McLaughlin
                    and Korkegi.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d552-f1" n="84" xml:id="d552-f1-content">
                <p>F. W. Utz, Executive Vice President of the Rubber Development Corporation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d552-f2" n="85" xml:id="d552-f2-content">
                <p>Harri J. Korkegi, representative of the Rubber Development Corporation in
                    Brazil.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
